# Istanbul Plus Django Project - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview

This is a Django e-commerce project for Istanbul Plus, featuring:

- Modern responsive design with Bootstrap 5.3.0
- RTL/LTR language support (Persian/English)
- Dark/Light theme system
- Modular template architecture
- Static file optimization

## Django Template Guidelines

### Template Tag Best Practices

1. **Always use proper template tag syntax:**

   ```django
   {% load static %}
   {% block extra_css %}{% endblock %}
   {% include "components/navbar.html" %}
   ```

2. **Avoid nested template tags:**

   ```django
   <!-- ❌ WRONG - Nested with tags cause syntax errors -->
   {% with context="navbar" %}
     {% with size="medium" %}
       {% include "components/logo.html" %}
     {% endwith %}
   {% endwith %}

   <!-- ✅ CORRECT - Use direct parameters -->
   {% include "components/logo.html" with size="medium" logo_context="navbar" %}
   ```

3. **Template block formatting:**

   ```django
   <!-- ❌ WRONG - Split across lines -->
   {% block extra_css %}{% endblock
   %}

   <!-- ✅ CORRECT - Single line or properly formatted -->
   {% block extra_css %}{% endblock %}
   ```

4. **Reserved parameter names to avoid:**
   - `context` (conflicts with Django's internal context)
   - Use `logo_context`, `card_context`, etc. instead

### Template Structure

- **Base template**: `templates/base.html` - Main layout with includes
- **Components**: `templates/components/` - Reusable UI components
- **Includes**: `templates/includes/` - Head sections, scripts, etc.
- **Pages**: `templates/[app_name]/` - App-specific templates

### Required Template Blocks

Every template extending `base.html` should use these blocks:

```django
{% block title %}Page Title{% endblock %}
{% block extra_css %}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}{% endblock %}
{% block extra_js %}{% endblock %}
```

## Theme System Guidelines

### Theme Management

1. **DO NOT modify theme files directly:**

   - `static/js/theme-manager.js` - Core theme logic
   - `static/js/theme-debug.js` - Debug panel (disabled in production)
   - `static/js/theme-test.js` - Testing utilities (disabled in production)

2. **Theme switching is handled automatically:**

   - Users can toggle between light/dark themes
   - Theme preference is saved in localStorage
   - System respects user's OS theme preference

3. **CSS Variables for theming:**

   ```css
   :root {
     --color-primary: #667eea;
     --color-secondary: #764ba2;
     --background-primary: #ffffff;
     --text-primary: #333333;
   }

   [data-theme="dark"] {
     --background-primary: #1a1a1a;
     --text-primary: #ffffff;
   }
   ```

### Avoiding Theme Issues

1. **Don't hardcode colors:**

   ```css
   /* ❌ WRONG */
   .my-element {
     color: #333;
     background: #fff;
   }

   /* ✅ CORRECT */
   .my-element {
     color: var(--text-primary);
     background: var(--background-primary);
   }
   ```

2. **Use theme-aware components:**

   ```django
   <!-- ✅ CORRECT - Logo component handles themes automatically -->
   {% include "components/logo.html" with size="medium" logo_context="navbar" %}
   ```

3. **Test both themes:**
   - Always test components in both light and dark themes
   - Ensure proper contrast ratios
   - Verify readability in both modes

## Static Files Management

### File Organization

```
static/
├── css/
│   ├── base/           # Core styles (fonts, variables, reset)
│   ├── components/     # Component-specific styles
│   ├── layouts/        # Page layout styles
│   └── utilities/      # Helper classes
├── js/
│   ├── theme-manager.js    # Theme system (DO NOT MODIFY)
│   ├── navigation.js       # Navigation functionality
│   └── [component].js      # Component-specific scripts
├── img/
│   ├── Istanbulplusir-logo-highquality.png
│   ├── Istanbulplusir-logo-lowquality.png
│   └── [other images]
└── fonts/
    └── bootstrap-icons.woff2
```

### Static File Usage

```django
<!-- ✅ CORRECT - Use static template tag -->
{% load static %}
<img src="{% static 'img/logo.png' %}" alt="Logo" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{% static 'css/main.css' %}" />
```

## Component Guidelines

### Logo Component

```django
<!-- Usage examples -->
{% include "components/logo.html" with size="small" quality="high" logo_context="navbar" %}
{% include "components/logo.html" with size="large" quality="low" logo_context="hero" show_text=false %}
```

**Parameters:**

- `size`: "small" (24px), "medium" (32px), "large" (48px), "xlarge" (64px)
- `quality`: "high" (highquality.png), "low" (lowquality.png)
- `logo_context`: "navbar", "footer", "hero", "card"
- `show_text`: true/false (default: true)
- `text_class`: CSS classes for text styling

### Navigation Component

- Responsive navbar with mobile menu
- Logo integration
- Theme toggle button
- Language switcher (RTL/LTR)

### Footer Component

- Multi-column layout
- Social media links
- Logo integration
- Copyright information

## Development Guidelines

### Code Style

1. **HTML**: Use semantic elements, proper indentation
2. **CSS**: Use CSS custom properties, mobile-first approach
3. **JavaScript**: ES6+, async/await, proper error handling
4. **Python**: PEP 8, type hints, docstrings

### Performance

1. **Images**: Use appropriate formats (WebP, PNG, JPG)
2. **CSS**: Minify for production, use critical CSS
3. **JavaScript**: Lazy load non-critical scripts
4. **Fonts**: Use system fonts, avoid external font loading

### Accessibility

1. **ARIA labels**: Proper labeling for screen readers
2. **Keyboard navigation**: All interactive elements accessible
3. **Color contrast**: WCAG AA compliance
4. **Focus management**: Visible focus indicators

## Common Issues & Solutions

### Template Syntax Errors

- **Problem**: `Unclosed tag on line X: 'block'`
- **Solution**: Ensure `{% endblock %}` is on the same line or properly formatted
- **CRITICAL**: Never split `{% endblock %}` across multiple lines - this causes persistent syntax errors
- **Example**:

  ```django
  <!-- ❌ WRONG - Causes persistent errors -->
  {% block extra_css %}{% endblock
  %}

  <!-- ✅ CORRECT - Single line -->
  {% block extra_css %}{% endblock %}
  ```

### Theme Not Working

- **Problem**: Theme toggle not responding
- **Solution**: Check if theme-manager.js is loaded, verify localStorage

### Static Files Not Loading

- **Problem**: 404 errors for CSS/JS files
- **Solution**: Run `python manage.py collectstatic`, check STATIC_URL setting

### Logo Not Displaying

- **Problem**: Logo component showing broken image
- **Solution**: Verify logo files exist in static/img/, check file permissions

## Testing Checklist

- [ ] Template syntax validation (`python manage.py check`)
- [ ] Static files loading correctly
- [ ] Theme switching works in both directions
- [ ] Responsive design on mobile/tablet/desktop
- [ ] RTL/LTR language switching
- [ ] Logo displays in all contexts
- [ ] Navigation works on all devices
- [ ] Forms submit correctly
- [ ] JavaScript errors in console

## File Modification Guidelines

### Files to NEVER modify directly:

- `static/js/theme-manager.js` - Core theme system
- `templates/base.html` - Use includes instead
- `settings/base.py` - Use environment-specific settings

### Files safe to modify:

- `templates/[app]/` - App-specific templates
- `static/css/components/` - Component styles
- `static/js/[component].js` - Component scripts
- `templates/components/` - Reusable components

## Deployment Notes

- Run `python manage.py collectstatic` before deployment
- Ensure all static files are properly served
- Test theme functionality in production environment
- Verify RTL/LTR switching works correctly
- Check mobile responsiveness

## Support

For issues related to:

- Template syntax: Check Django template documentation
- Theme system: Review theme-manager.js comments
- Static files: Verify Django static files configuration
- Components: Check component documentation in templates/components/
